			</_properties>
			<_rmmServerID type="a">1143278_pDnuAbU4Ee6Ru6Ifm1D6NA</_rmmServerID>
			<_name type="a">SAF_O6_SKRD</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">10.19.2026::6:31:38</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\fbidis\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1031{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}\viewkind4\uc1\pard\ltrpar\cf1\fs20 Implementation of \cf2\ul\protect Stakeholder Requirement Definition Viewpoint \cf0\ulnone\protect0 \par \pard\ltrpar Purpose:\par \pard\ltrpar The Stakeholder Requirement Definition Viewpoint specifies all capabilities, functions and properties, that the intended solution shall possess or expose from the perspective of the Stakeholders. The Stakeholder Requirement Definition Viewpoint also captures constraints for the system to be developed from stakeholders perspective.\par \pard\ltrpar Presentation:\par \pard\ltrpar A tabular format lisiting\par {\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ltrpar\fi-360\li360 unique requirement ID, text, and attributes,\par {\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ltrpar\fi-360\li360 traceability reference to justifying model artefacts, e.g. operational stories, operational capabilities, identified concerns of stakeholders, and compliance statements\par \pard\ltrpar Note: Stakeholder Requirements are to be structured in a way that the Stakeholder behind the Requirement is identifiable. When appropriate, the relationships between identified Stakeholder Requirements are and the justifying model artefacts, Operational Story, Operational Capability, Operational Performer, Operational Process, and Operational Exchange are presented.\par {\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ltrpar\fi-360\li360 &quot;One Requirement Package for each Stakeholder&quot; is a best-practice modeling rule. A package contains the Requirements specific for one Stakeholder.\par {\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ltrpar\fi-360\li360 Even if different Stakeholders may have intersecting interests and / or concerns resulting in a similar set of Requirements, each Stakeholder shall have its own set managed in a dedicated Requirement Package. Requirements must not be shared due to their different life cycles. Resolving duplications and conflicts is subject of the requirement analysis resulting in an agreed and consolidated set of System Requirements.\par}</_textRTF>
				<Hyperlinks type="c">
					<IRPYRawContainer type="e">
						<IExternalHyperlink type="e">
							<_name type="a">Stakeholder Requirement Definition Viewpoint </_name>
							<_textType type="a">FREE</_textType>
							<_target type="a">https://saf.gfse.org/userdoc/Operational Domain/Stakeholder Requirement Definition Viewpoint</_target>
						</IExternalHyperlink>
						
					</IRPYRawContainer>
				</Hyperlinks>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">10.19.2026::6:31:38</_modifiedTime>
			<_lastID type="a">3</_lastID>
