			<_rmmServerID type="a">1143194_pDnuAbU4Ee6Ru6Ifm1D6NA</_rmmServerID>
			<_name type="a">SAF_P4_PIEX</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">10.19.2026::6:31:38</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\fbidis\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1031{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}\viewkind4\uc1\pard\ltrpar\cf1\fs20 Implementation of \cf2\ul\protect Physical Internal Exchange Viewpoint \cf0\ulnone\protect0 \par \pard\ltrpar Purpose:\par \pard\ltrpar The Physical Internal Exchange Viewpoint serves for the identification and definition of interfaces of elements of the physical system. also, the delegation of system element interfaces to the physical system boundary interfaces is covered.\par \pard\ltrpar The Physical Internal Exchange Viewpoint\par {\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ltrpar\fi-360\li360 identifies system element interfaces on a physical level\par {\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ltrpar\fi-360\li360 states to which other physical elements the interfaces are connected to\par {\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ltrpar\fi-360\li360 assigns physical interface definitions to interfaces\par {\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ltrpar\fi-360\li360 defines the usage of interfaces, e.g., if only a subset of the interfaces is used\par {\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ltrpar\fi-360\li360 defines the delegation of physical system element interfaces to physical system boundary interfaces\par \pard\ltrpar Presentations:\par \pard\ltrpar  \par {\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ltrpar\fi-360\li360 One or more IBDs featuring the SOI boundary, the parts representing physical elements of the SOI. At the SOI boundary, the interfaces of the SOI represented as proxy ports. At the parts, proxy ports representing the SOI parts interfaces. Binding Connectors for each identified SOI interface delegated to physical SOI elements interfaces. connectors representing connections between interfaces of SOI parts. Item flows are defined for each planned exchange on the identified interfaces. Note: Please use more than one IBD focused on different areas of interest to keep the view comprehensive. Note: Ports may be nested to organize interfaces, but it is recommended to use only only one level.\par {\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ltrpar\fi-360\li360 A Table representing the content or part of the ibd content.\par}</_textRTF>
				<Hyperlinks type="c">
					<IRPYRawContainer type="e">
						<IExternalHyperlink type="e">
							<_name type="a">Physical Internal Exchange Viewpoint </_name>
							<_textType type="a">FREE</_textType>
							<_target type="a">https://saf.gfse.org/userdoc/Physical Domain/Physical Internal Exchange Viewpoint</_target>
						</IExternalHyperlink>
						
					</IRPYRawContainer>
				</Hyperlinks>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">10.19.2026::6:31:38</_modifiedTime>
