			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">10.19.2026::6:31:38</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\fbidis\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1031{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}\viewkind4\uc1\pard\ltrpar\cf1\fs20 Implementation of \cf2\ul\protect System Functional Breakdown Structure Viewpoint \cf0\ulnone\protect0 \par \pard\ltrpar Purpose:\par \pard\ltrpar The System Functional Breakdown Structure Viewpoint defines the structured, modular functional breakdown of the SOI beginning with System Processes, over identified System Functions further refined down to System Partial Functions. The reuse of System Functions, and System Partial Functions over Function Trees of the SOI is facilitated. \par \pard\ltrpar Presentations:\par \pard\ltrpar  \par {\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ltrpar\fi-360\li360 One or more more block definition diagrams (BDD) featuring activities representing System Processes, System Functions, System Partial Functions, and their aggregation composing the functional breakdown structure.\par {\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ltrpar\fi-360\li360 Tool specific analysis diagram featuring the relationships between System Processes, System Functions, and System Partial Functions.\par}</_textRTF>
				<Hyperlinks type="c">
					<IRPYRawContainer type="e">
						<IExternalHyperlink type="e">
							<_name type="a">System Functional Breakdown Structure Viewpoint </_name>
							<_textType type="a">FREE</_textType>
							<_target type="a">https://saf.gfse.org/userdoc/Conceptual Domain/System Functional Breakdown Structure Viewpoint</_target>
						</IExternalHyperlink>
						
					</IRPYRawContainer>
				</Hyperlinks>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
