			</_properties>
			<_rmmServerID type="a">2261752_pDnuAbU4Ee6Ru6Ifm1D6NA</_rmmServerID>
			<_name type="a">SAF_C4_SIEX</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">10.19.2026::6:31:38</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\fbidis\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1031{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}\viewkind4\uc1\pard\ltrpar\cf1\fs20 Implementation of \cf2\ul\protect System Internal Exchange Viewpoint \cf0\ulnone\protect0 \par \pard\ltrpar Purpose:\par \pard\ltrpar The System Internal Exchange Viewpoint serves for the identification and definition of interfaces of elements of the conceptual system. also, the delegation of system element interfaces to the conceptual system boundary interfaces is covered.\par \pard\ltrpar The System Internal Exchange Viewpoint\par {\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ltrpar\fi-360\li360 identifies system element interfaces on a conceptual level\par {\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ltrpar\fi-360\li360 states to which other conceptual elements the interfaces are connected to\par {\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ltrpar\fi-360\li360 assigns conceptual interface definitions to interfaces\par {\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ltrpar\fi-360\li360 defines the usage of interfaces, e.g., if only a subset of the interfaces is used \par {\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\ltrpar\fi-360\li360 defines the delegation of conceptual system element interfaces to the conceptual system boundary interfaces\par \pard\ltrpar Presentation:\par \pard\ltrpar One or more IBDs featuring the SOI boundary, the conceptual elements of the SOI, as well as the connectors for each identified SOI interface delegation to conceptual SOI elements. An interface is a connection resource for hooking on the conceptual SOI elements to other conceptual SOI elements. Item flows are defined for each exchange on the identified interface.\par \pard\ltrpar Note: Please use more than one IBD focused on different areas of interest to keep the view comprehensive.\par}</_textRTF>
				<Hyperlinks type="c">
					<IRPYRawContainer type="e">
						<IExternalHyperlink type="e">
							<_name type="a">System Internal Exchange Viewpoint </_name>
							<_textType type="a">FREE</_textType>
							<_target type="a">https://saf.gfse.org/userdoc/Conceptual Domain/System Internal Exchange Viewpoint</_target>
						</IExternalHyperlink>
						
					</IRPYRawContainer>
				</Hyperlinks>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">10.19.2026::6:31:38</_modifiedTime>
